### 3. US federal regulation — public domain, and named separately for that reason

[`working/leads6/K4-corporate-actions-source-and-conventions.md`](working/leads6/K4-corporate-actions-source-and-conventions.md)
at `:269-292` reproduces **1,782 characters**: the complete enumeration of 17 CFR
§ 240.10b-17(b)(1), read from the eCFR. US federal regulation is **not subject to copyright**, and
that passage is here in full for the same reason it could be: the argument is that the rule lists
declaration, record and payment dates and never mentions an ex-date, and a partial quotation would
not establish it.

This is worth separating from class 2 rather than lumping in with it, and the same file shows why:
the FINRA UPC FAQ quoted twenty lines further down is **not** public domain. FINRA is a private
self-regulatory organisation. Adjacency in a document is not shared status.

