## Pseudonymous authors

[`15-reddit-mined.md`](docs/research/Prop-Firm-080926/15-reddit-mined.md) attributes specific claims
to **27 pseudonymous handles**, and several of those attributions are evaluative — a claim is named,
and then refuted. The file's own header says what it is (`:16-19`): *nothing there is evidence*,
every row is a hypothesis with a falsification criterion.

Three things follow, stated here rather than left to be inferred:

- Forum authors are cited by **public handle and permalink only**, for claims they chose to publish
  publicly. **No real name, email address, employer or location is attached to any of them**, and
  none was sought.
- The evaluation is **of the claim, not of the person**. Where a post is called overfitted or
  arithmetically wrong, that is a statement about the numbers in the post. Where a post is good it
  is said so, at the same length.
- **A request from a cited author to remove an attribution will be honoured.** Open an issue or
  contact the author of this repository; the handle and the link come out and the claim stays or
  goes with them.

---

## Removal and correction

Any rights holder — a firm whose terms are quoted, a publisher, a forum author — who wants a
passage shortened or removed should say so, and it will be. Corrections to what a source is said to
have written are treated the same way as any other error in this repository: fixed, and recorded in
writing rather than quietly edited.
